DS3D common is the shared runtime for every other DS3D module. It provides the
`ds3d::datamap` container, the 2D/3D frame wrappers, the abstract data-process
interfaces (`ds3d::dataloader`, `ds3d::datafilter`, `ds3d::datarender`,
`ds3d::databridge`, `ds3d::datamixer`), the YAML configuration helpers and the
CUDA/error-handling utilities.

DS3D is framework agnostic. There is no gstreamer/Glib dependency in this
library. Any framework could simply wrap DS3D modules.

`libnvds_3d_common.so` is built from these source files. The only exported
C-API is `NvDs3d_CreateDataHashMap`, which backs the `ds3d::datamap`
implementation; everything else is header-only and consumed from
`includes/ds3d/common`.

The public headers are not duplicated here — they are installed from
`includes/ds3d/common` and included as `<ds3d/common/...>`:

    ds3d/common/common.h                 core types and error codes
    ds3d/common/hpp/datamap.hpp          datamap guard wrapper
    ds3d/common/hpp/frame.hpp            2D/3D frame guard wrappers
    ds3d/common/hpp/yaml_config.hpp      YAML component-config parsing
    ds3d/common/impl/impl_*.h            base classes for custom modules
    ds3d/common/helper/*.h               CUDA, queue and timing helpers

Every other DS3D module links against this library, so it must be built and
installed first.

More details, refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for section of "DeepStream 3D Custom Manual".
https://nvidia-deepstream.docs.buildwithfern.com/deepstream/9.2/text/DS_3D_Custom_Manual

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- CUDA Runtime

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing this lib:
- Export CUDA_VER, then build. sudo -E keeps the variable for make.
  $ export CUDA_VER=13.2 # x86, Jetson and SBSA. For IGX Thor, CUDA_VER=13.0
  $ make && sudo -E make install
- Verify `libnvds_3d_common.so` exist and installed well.

NOTE: Compiling does not need root. Install with `sudo -E` so CUDA_VER is kept. Skip sudo when already root (for example inside a container).
